<h2 id="two">Two completely different prices for the same shower</h2>
<p>This is the thing worth understanding before you take a single appointment, and almost nobody in this industry will tell you: <strong>the panels in a $3,000 job and the panels in a $20,000 job are frequently the same panels</strong>, from the same manufacturer, in the same finish, made in the same factory.</p>
<p>What differs is everything wrapped around them.</p>
<p>A shower wall kit is a manufactured product with a wholesale price. That price does not change much between buyers. What changes enormously is the commercial structure through which it reaches you: whether you buy it and hire a fitter, or whether a company sells you a finished bathroom on a single contract with a warranty, a crew, a project manager, a financing partner, and a marketing budget that had to find you in the first place.</p>
<p>Both are legitimate businesses. Neither is a scam. But the price difference between them is roughly three to five times, and that is a lot of money to spend without knowing which one you are buying.</p>
<div class="callout"><p><strong>The one question that cuts through all of it:</strong> &ldquo;Which manufacturer and model panel are you installing, and what thickness?&rdquo; A company confident in its product answers immediately. A company that will not answer is telling you that the product is not what you are paying for.</p></div>

<h2 id="est">Estimate your opening</h2>
<div class="tool" id="est">
<span class="eyebrow on-dark">Estimator</span>
<h3>Price your opening on all three paths</h3>
<p class="intro">The same shower has three very different prices depending on who buys the panel and who fits it. This prices all three at once so you can see what each path is actually charging you for.</p>
<div class="t-in c4">
<div><label for="e-w">Width (in)</label><input id="e-w" type="number" value="60" min="24" max="144" step="1"></div>
<div><label for="e-d">Depth (in)</label><input id="e-d" type="number" value="32" min="20" max="72" step="1"></div>
<div><label for="e-h">Panel height</label><select id="e-h">
<option value="60">60&Prime; (tub surround)</option><option value="72">72&Prime;</option>
